-- title:
--   Ordinary line for the λ-adic representation of a newform
-- statement:
--   Fix $M\ge 1$ and a cusp form $g$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices, and the recursions $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}-p\,a_{p^r}$ for $p\nmid M$, $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}$ for $p\mid M$) and no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ carries a normalised eigenform with the same $a_\ell$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals with $\lambda\in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $M$, and $\mathcal O'$ a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb C$ from the Hecke algebra of level $M$, weight $2$ away from $S\setminus\{\lambda\}$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$ and the $U_q$ with $q$ prime, $q\mid M$, $q\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$), with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for all such $\ell$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ into $\mathcal O'$. Assume $\lambda\nmid M$ and that $\iota\chi_g(T_\lambda)$ is a unit of $\mathcal O'$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\lambda$ a nonunit of $P$. Then there is a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O''$ with finite residue field, finite as an $\mathcal O'$-algebra, with $\mathcal O'\to\mathcal O''$ local and injective, and a $\lambda$-adically continuous representation $\rho$ of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ on a free $\mathcal O''$-module $V$ of rank $2$ (continuity: for each $n$ some finite subextension of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ has its pointwise stabiliser acting trivially modulo $\mathfrak m^nV$) such that: for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting on its residue field by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\iota\chi_g(T_\ell)X+\ell$; and there are a line $L=\mathcal O''b_0$ spanned by the first vector of some $\mathcal O''$-basis $(b_0,b_1)$ of $V$ and a unit $\alpha\in\mathcal O''$ with $\alpha^2-\iota\chi_g(T_\lambda)\alpha+\lambda=0$ such that $L$ is stable under the decomposition group of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, every element of the inertia subgroup of $P$ (viewed inside the decomposition group) acts trivially on $V/L$, and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\lambda$ for $P$ satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v-\alpha v\in L$ for all $v\in V$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility statement, in existence form, for the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two newform at a prime $\lambda$ of good reduction at which the form is ordinary: Frobenius characteristic polynomials $X^2-a_\ell X+\ell$ away from the bad set, together with an ordinary line whose unramified quotient carries Frobenius acting by the unit root of $X^2-a_\lambda X+\lambda$. It feeds the downstream statements producing ordinary representations from newforms, among them [`GaloisRepAdic.exists_ordinaryLine_frobenius_sub_unitRoot_smul_mem_of_isNewform_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.exists_ordinaryLine_frobenius_sub_unitRoot_smul_mem_of_isNewform_of_not_dvd) and [`CuspForm.exists_galoisRepAdic_of_point_stableLine_frobenius_sub_smul_mem_of_isUnit_U`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_galoisRepAdic_of_point_stableLine_frobenius_sub_smul_mem_of_isUnit_U).
